      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To further investigate resource contention and potential race conditions, you should first ensure that your Jenkins server has sufficient resources to meet the demand of parallel build executions. Monitoring real-time metrics and running a resource usage analysis during the unit test stage can help identify any choke points. Implement queue management strategies, such as prioritizing certain builds or scaling your Jenkins agents dynamically based on workload. Consider also using dependencies strategically within your Jenkinsfile to avoid race conditions. If the problem is related to network issues, investigate network performance, and ensure that the unit tests' dependencies are accessible consistently with proper caching mechanisms when possible. Expanding the test environment to newer hardware could also shine a light on whether the issue is tied to specific hardware resources.",
