    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Although it might seem unusual, Jenkins agents behaving unpredictably can indeed be caused by a hidden background task or resource leaks. Investigate using tools designed to monitor the Jenkins agent processes in greater detail. Tools like Process Explorer can help you see the memory and resource allocation for the processes that Jenkins operates. In addition, check for the presence of any detached or orphaned processes that might be running unexpectedly and examine the Jenkins agent logs for any clues about rogue background tasks. To detect memory leaks, you can employ diagnostic tools such as LeakSanitizer or similar. Consider also reviewing any custom scripts or setup adds-in in your Jenkins environment as they might be altering the expected behavior. Furthermore, a clean reinstall of the Jenkins agent itself might help, as this can reset any peculiar or erratic states that have been overlooked.",
